ill be Australian big four banks who have a 100% correlation with the AUD/JPY cross rate," says Southern Cross Equities director Charlie Aitken, who predicted BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in his morning newsletter. Index breaks through May 13 high at 4652.8, leaving index heading for next Fibonacci target at 4710 (61.8% retracement of April/June fall), according to Dow Jones Newswires technical analysis. (david.rogers1@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0209 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY, EUR/JPY, JPY crosses jump after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. While many market participants had speculated that Kan win Tuesday in DPJ party president election against Ozawa, who was viewed as more vocal proponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , would lessen likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , senior dealer at major \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  bank says "even from when he was finance minister, it was clear Kan wanted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Two traders say MOF was spotted selling Y200 billion To Y300 billion vs USD. USD/JPY hits 84.30 vs earlier low of 82.87, while EUR/JPY jumps to 109.35 from 107.74 earlier; AUD/JPY also sharply higher while EUR/USD has moved down. (andrew.monahan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0205 GMT [Dow Jones] China government bonds up amid easing concerns over inflation after NDRC vice director Zhang Xiaoqiang said yesterday China can still achieve its targeted annual CPI increase of around 3.0% despite CPI rising by near 2-year high in August. "Zhang's comment strengthens expectations Beijing won't introduce interest rate hikes this year as the inflation growth will slow down in the coming months," says Shenzhen-based trader with local fund. Shanghai Stock Exchange government bond index at 126.89 vs 126.87 last close, tipped to test 127.0 by Friday. (ming.wang@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0205 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei 225 futures jump 1.7% to 9410 vs intraday low of 9140 on news \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan Ministry of Finance intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders say. "It caught us by surprise," says Japanese brokerage manager, adding futures buying also driving up cash market (Nikkei up 1.8% midday). Fund manager at U.S. asset management firm says investors had been speculating government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon as USD/JPY was trading below 83 this morning. Adds both Nikkei and Nikkei futures may trade above 9500 in coming days. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0201 GMT [Dow Jones] Vietnam shares +0.3% at 450.21 as investors continue to buy on expectations of solid 3Q earnings, though concerns over high interest rates remain; index off 451.14 earlier high. "As prices of many blue chips have fallen significantly in recent weeks, some players are coming back to buy," says Hanoi-based trader. Adds volume thin because of lack of fresh news on how \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act to help boost cash liquidity in economy. Expects key index in 448-455 range. (phammuoi.nguyen@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/CNY falls sharply again after PBOC set USD/CNY central parity rate at record low (6.7250 vs 6.7378 yesterday) for 4th consecutive session; on OTC, USD/CNY at 6.7331, off 6.7330 fresh intraday low under current system shortly after open, vs 6.7463 last close; "The dollar index dropped below the 200-day moving average of around 81.70 overnight. Given that, the central parity isn't overly low," says Shanghai-based trader at foreign bank. Adds magnitude of fixing decline has been around 120-130 points each day, further downside likely. "The U.S. Congressional hearing on the yuan matter is imminent, and China's recent strong data give foreign countries more reasons to question why the yuan hasn't risen much." USD/CNY tipped in 6.7250-6.7400 range for session. Offshore, 1-year USD/CNY NDF at 6.6370/6.6400 vs 6.6550/6.6600 late yesterday. (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei up 1.9% at 9473.48, off high of 9489.32, rising sharply from negative territory, after USD/JPY rises sharply to near 84 (now 83.97) as dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Finance Minister Noda confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at news conference currently in progess, but did not specify amount. "It may serve as a temporary brake on the stronger yen trend," says Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities. But notes Nikkei rebound may unlikely to last since stronger yen trend based mostly on U.S. economic conditions. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely higher after week-long holiday as investors expected to continue buying stocks to catch up with recent gains on Wall Street, dealers say. "Eventhough (U.S. stocks) fell slightly overnight, I think sentiment on local stocks will remain positive," says Indo Primer Sekuritas analyst Dang Maulida. Tips main index to test 3,250 resistance vs last close at 3,230.89 (+0.4%); support pegged at 3,200. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com) [ 09-14-10 2218ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0001m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
