ystem shortly after open, vs 6.7463 last close; "The dollar index dropped below the 200-day moving average of around 81.70 overnight. Given that, the central parity isn't overly low," says Shanghai-based trader at foreign bank. Adds magnitude of fixing decline has been around 120-130 points each day, further downside likely. "The U.S. Congressional hearing on the yuan matter is imminent, and China's recent strong data give foreign countries more reasons to question why the yuan hasn't risen much." USD/CNY tipped in 6.7250-6.7400 range for session. Offshore, 1-year USD/CNY NDF at 6.6370/6.6400 vs 6.6550/6.6600 late yesterday. (joy.shaw@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] Nikkei up 1.9% at 9473.48, off high of 9489.32, rising sharply from negative territory, after USD/JPY rises sharply to near 84 (now 83.97) as dealers say \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. Finance Minister Noda confirmed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at news conference currently in progess, but did not specify amount. "It may serve as a temporary brake on the stronger yen trend," says Yutaka Miura, senior technical analyst at Mizuho Securities. But notes Nikkei rebound may unlikely to last since stronger yen trend based mostly on U.S. economic conditions. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0200 GMT [Dow Jones] Indonesia shares likely higher after week-long holiday as investors expected to continue buying stocks to catch up with recent gains on Wall Street, dealers say. "Eventhough (U.S. stocks) fell slightly overnight, I think sentiment on local stocks will remain positive," says Indo Primer Sekuritas analyst Dang Maulida. Tips main index to test 3,250 resistance vs last close at 3,230.89 (+0.4%); support pegged at 3,200. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0155 GMT [Dow Jones] September HSI futures +0.3% at 21,760, suggests cash market will open modestly higher. Contract ended yesterday at 2-point discount to cash, vs September fair value about 7-point discount, suggesting investors anticipating HSI's near-term upside may be limited, as index already risen 9 out of 10 sessions, may need to take breather. September open interest decreases 1,073 lots to 102,213. (robert.li@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0154 GMT [Dow Jones] China shares down early as property developers extend losses amid unabated concerns over second round of property tightening. Shanghai Composite Index last down 0.3% at 2680.02, tipped to stay in tight 2650-2700 range for now. "The uncertainty over whether Beijing will launch further tightening measures for the property market continues to weigh on developers and banks," says Deng Wenyuan at Soochow Securities. Adds market extra cautious ahead of next week's 3-day mid-autumn festival holiday, as China has chosen holiday periods to launch new policies in past. Among actives, \uc2 China Vanke\uc2  (000002.SZ) down 0.5% at CNY8.26, \uc2 Poly Real Estate Group\uc2  (600048.SH) down 1.5% at CNY11.22; \uc2 China Merchants Bank\uc2  (600036.SH) also down 1.4% at CNY13.18. Shenzhen index last down 0.4% at 1202.47. (jean.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0148 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD lower at 31.700 vs over 5-week closing high 31.815 yesterday, marking 6th-straight session of losses, as regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  boosted by lower USD/CNY fixing, says local bank trader. "If the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain biased up, the pair is likely to try the key 31.500 or even 31.300 supports in the near term," he says. Tips pair in wide 31.600-31.800 band for day. (mason.wu@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0136 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/HKD lower on weaker USD offshore, says senior trader at local bank. Tips pair in 7.7620-7.7690 band near term. "I expect the pair to maintain its downward bias, tracking another record low fixing in USD/CNY today. The recent strength of local stocks could attract inflows, lending support to the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." Pair last 7.7664 vs 7.7673 yesterday. (chester.yung@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0134 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI down 0.2% at 1471.22 as investors lock in gains from market's recent rally to 32-month highs; dealers say retreat not surprising as KLCI had reached overbought territory. TA Research says KLCI's 14-day RSI was at the highest in over 2 years, an "extreme overbought reading"; dealers peg immediate support at 1465. Still, pullback likely temporary as market's longer-term uptrend remains intact amid positive domestic economic, earnings growth prospects, dealers say. Among decliners, Jerneh (6394.KU) down 4.9% at MYR3.12 on concerns over company's future following sale of core insurance business, Genting (3182.KU) down 0.9% at MYR9.90 on profit-taking after strong gains yesterday. Among gainers, Gamuda (5398.KU) +1.4% at MYR3.75 after being picked to be KLCI component stock, replacing soon-to-be-delisted Tanjong (2267.KU). (benjamin.low@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0133 GMT [Dow Jones] Big U.S. bank selling good amounts of EUR/USD from 1.3010 this morning, says Singapore-based dealer; EUR/USD last at 1.2999. (jerry.tan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0133 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR steady at 8,965 on good 2-way interest around level, dealers say. "The dollar's general weakness is capping the pair, but many players are also covering their short-dollar positions," dealer says; adds suspected Bank Indonesia dollar buying around IDR8,955 yesterday also discourages players from pushing pair below 8,960-8,975 range tipped for day. (i-made.sentana@dowjones.com) [ 09-14-10 2204ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100915e69f0001a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
