\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Euro Tops $1.30 After Data; Yen At 15-year High\b0\par\par\uc2 By Deborah Levine  \par \uc2 856 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 22:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global News Select\par \uc2 DJON\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar dropped against all the major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday after reports showed U.S. retail sales and business inventories rose more than expected.\par \par \uc2 The data eased investors' worries about the outlook for the global economy, making them more willing to buy riskier assets, including stocks and commodities, and moving away from assets considered safer, such as the greenback.\par \par \uc2 "Risk-on nowadays is to actually buy the euro," said Dean Popplewell, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Oanda.\par \par \uc2 Separately, the Japanese yen jumped to a fresh 15-year high against the U.S. dollar after Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan survived a party leadership challenge from Ichiro Ozawa, easing concerns about the potential for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index (DXY), which tracks the performance of the greenback against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traded at 81.064, down from 81.914 in late North American trading Monday.\par \par \uc2 The euro (CUR_EURUSD) turned up to buy $1.3024, up from around $1.2870 Monday. It hasn't topped $1.39 intraday since early August.\par \par \uc2 The single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turned up versus the yen to \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A5108.04 from \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A5107.63 Monday.\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded as low as 82.970 yen (CUR_USDYEN), its lowest level versus the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since May 1995 and down from \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A583.66 in late North American trading on Monday.\par \par \uc2 In recent action, the dollar changed hands at \u194\'00\'C2\u165\'00\'A583.13.\par \par \uc2 The dollar also fell versus the British pound, Canadian dollar and hit the lowest this year against the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 The dollar turned lower versus the euro after a report showed U.S. business inventories jumped 1% in July.\par \par \uc2 Treasury prices rose sharply and gold futures jumped to settle at a new record high.\par \par \uc2 The dollar had been a little better versus the euro earlier after the U.S. Commerce Department said retail sales rose in August more than some analysts forecast.\par \par \uc2 "The better-than-expected retail sales report provides additional reason to believe that perhaps the slowdown in the economy will prove to be just that and not a prelude to a double-dip recession," said Jim Baird, chief investment strategist for Plante Moran Financial Advisors.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were also swayed by reports that the Federal Reserve may begin a new program of buying U.S. debt. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying its own country's debt is often known as quantitative easing, leading maybe to dub the potential new efforts QE2.\par \par \uc2 "A string of stories that suggest the Fed is closer to QE2 than the market might appreciate, offers by far the best explanation for the price action in the last 24 hours, " said Alan Ruskin, global head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 . "The \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  impact looks likely to be dependent on whether Fed QE is perceived as pre-emptive and proactive, or late to the game."\par \par \uc2 If it's proactive when growth is merely subpar, QE will add to market confidence and encourage risk-taking, he said.\par \par \uc2 The growth takes a sharp turn down and deflation fears rise, it may be unclear if QE will work and so investors would seek safety, Ruskin said.\par \par \uc2 Japanese election\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister Kan, head of the ruling Democratic Party of Japan, is regarded as more fiscally conservative and less likely to support \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen, amid concerns that a stronger yen is bad for Japanese international businesses and exporters.\par \par \uc2 "Prime Minister Kan succeeded in holding off the challenge at the DPJ leadership contest, easing the threat on the margins of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which helped lift the yen to new 15-year highs against the dollar," said strategists at \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The election doesn't close the door on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said one analyst.\par \par \uc2 Perceptions that Kan won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be proven wrong and that government action "could be just around the corner," said Flemming Nielsen, senior analyst at \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  in Copenhagen.\par \par \uc2 "In our view, we are now very close to a situation where \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have to do it alone without the support of Europe and the U.S. and hence the effectiveness of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is questionable," Nielsen wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 ZEW survey\par \par \uc2 The euro had been lower earlier after Germany's ZEW economic sentiment indicator posted an unexpectedly large drop, reflecting increased concerns about slower U.S. growth and unresolved sovereign-debt problems in the euro zone.\par \par \uc2 Although the ZEW gauge isn't viewed by economists as a reliable leading indicator, the survey "took some of the shine off the euro," said Geoffrey Yu, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 UBS\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Also, data showed that industrial production in the 16-nation euro zone and production was a little weaker than economists predicted.\par \par \uc2 The British pound (CUR_GBPUSD) rose 1.1% versus the greenback at $1.5567. It had been under pressure earlier. The U.K. Office for National Statistics said annual consumer price inflation was unchanged at 3.1% in August, while economists expected the inflation to slow. [ 09-14-10 1614ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJON000020100914e69e0006k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
