\par\par \b \uc2 Australia, NZ dollars leap as Japan sells yen\b0\par\par\uc2 704 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2010\par 00:44\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Aussie up 2 pct vs yen as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on US$/yen\par \par \uc2 * Aussie off two-year peak on US$, Kiwi near 7-week top\par \par \uc2 * RBNZ meets Thursday and seen skipping a hike this time\par \par \uc2 By Mantik Kusjanto and Wayne Cole\par \par \uc2 SYDNEY/WELLINGTON, Sept 15 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar jumped to a five-week peak against the yen on Wednesday, while holding not far from two-year highs on the U.S. dollar, as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The local dollar had already shot as far as $0.9457 <AUD=D4> offshore Tuesday, taking it back to heights held in July 2008 before the global financial crisis sent it crashing.\par \par \uc2 Then the Bank of Japan stepped in to sell the yen in an effort to restrain its export-sapping strength, and helped lift the Aussie 2 percent to 79.55 yen <AUDJPY=>.\par \par \uc2 The surprise \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was aimed at dragging the ailing U.S. dollar up from a 15-year low of 82.87 yen <JPY=> and proved enough to lift it to 84.85 late in the session. [ID:nECONJP]\par \par \uc2 As a result the Aussie pulled back slightly on the U.S. dollar to $0.9377 <AUD=D4>, but was still ahead by 5 percent for the month so far.\par \par \uc2 The next targets are highs from July 2008 at $0.9464, $0.9477 and $0.9529 and dealers are starting to talk of parity, though they have been disappointed repeatedly in the past.\par \par \uc2 The New Zealand dollar likewise jumped on the yen to 62.19 <NZDJPY=R>, from around 60.83. But it also backed off to <NZD=D4> $0.7326, from a seven-week high of $0.7395.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar had been hit by talk the Federal Reserve was moving closer to more quantitative easing.\par \par \uc2 "I still think the U.S. dollar weakness is going to continue. The kiwi, Aussie and euro remain a buy on dips at this stage," said Daniel Brdanovic, \uc2 HSBC\uc2  senior manager treasury.\par \par \uc2 The kiwi was seen supported from $0.7300, with resistance at the late July high of $0.7397, ahead of the 2010 high of $0.7447.\par \par \uc2 That was still a marked turnaround in fortunes as the kiwi had been as low as $0.7268 this week following data which showed housing and retail spending weak. [ID:nSGE68C05L] [ID:nWEL004161]\par \par \uc2 The kiwi shrugged off expectations that the Reserve Bank of NZ will keep rate steady on Thursday in the face of a sluggish recovery and shocks such as the Sept 4 earthquake. Market pricing sees only a 2 percent chance of a rate hike.\par \par \uc2 "A lot of it has already been priced in. Nobody is expecting a rate hike and most people have taken out rate hikes for the rest of the year," Brdanovic said. A Reuters poll sees cash rate at 3.25 percent at end of the year. [NZ/POLL]\par \par \uc2 The risk for the market would be if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes out with a rather hawkish statement.\par \par \uc2 NZ debt <0#NZTSY=> was firm, with yields 1 basis points lower in the short end.\par \par \uc2 Australian data out Wednesday were mixed, a change from the recent run of uniformly upbeat news. A measure of consumer sentiment surprised by falling 5 percent even though recent economic news had been very positive. [ID:nSDYFKE6FD]\par \par \uc2 Yet the level of confidence was still historically high and consistent with economic growth above 3 percent going forward.\par \par \uc2 New home starts rose a modest 0.8 percent in the second quarter but only because the previous quarter was revised up strongly to show an increase of 9.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 The level of new homes starts topped forecasts at a six-year high, which should underpin construction for a while yet.\par \par \uc2 The market is now looking to a speech by RBA Assistant Governor Philip Lowe on Thursday titled "The Development of Asia: Risk and Returns for Australia."\par \par \uc2 Australian three-year bond futures <YTTc1> were off 0.030 points at 95.230, while 10-year futures <YTCc1> eased 0.020 points to 94.915.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-AUSTRALIA-NEWZEALAND-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /BONDS (UPDATE2)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|AUF|ND|RNP|DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020100917e69e001iq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
