\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked For September 14\b0\par\par\uc2 1,807 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 09:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asia-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0700 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires. Please direct any questions or comments to asianewseds@dowjones.com.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME:\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: KAN BEATS BACK OZAWA CHALLENGE TO REMAIN JAPAN PM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan beat back a strong challenge to his hold on power Tuesday, defeating a challenge for ruling-party leadership from longtime powerbroker Ichiro Ozawa. (published 0646 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS YEN HITS NEW 15-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  threatened again Tuesday to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market after the yen pushed to a fresh 15-year high against the dollar, keeping traders on their toes ahead of a ruling party leadership election later in the day that could trigger more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA YUAN HITS FRESH MODERN-ERA HIGH VS DOLLAR TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit another high against the U.S. dollar Tuesday after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate lower for the third straight trading session amid the dollar's global weakness and growing U.S. pressure over Beijng's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =DATA SNAP: INDIA WHOLESALE PRICE INDEX UP 8.5% IN AUGUST \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's wholesale inflation stood at 8.5% based on the new index for measuring wholesale prices that was launched Tuesday. (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA AUGUST BUSINESS CONFIDENCE INDEX UP 9 POINTS TO +11 -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business confidence rose strongly in August, according to a survey released Tuesday, despite a period of political uncertainty as the country was left wondering what the make-up of the next government would be. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ RETAIL SALES NO IMPETUS FOR RBNZ TO HIKE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand retail sales fell in July, failing to meet expectations and giving little impetus for the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to start hiking the official cash rate before December. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BANK INDONESIA OFFICIAL: SEPT ON-YEAR INFLATION LIKELY BELOW 6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's on-year inflation in September will likely ease below 6%, from 6.44% in August, but the full-year target of 6% seems "hard to achieve," Bank Indonesia deputy governor Hartadi Sarwono said Tuesday. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ AUGUST MEDIAN HOUSE PRICE NZ$350,000 VS NZ$349,000 JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subdued home sales in August compared to July and relatively flat home prices, coupled with tepid retail sales data Tuesday, further underscore that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand will likely keep key rates on hold at 3.0% at Thursday's monetary-policy review. (published 2346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: PHILIPPINES REJECTS BIDS TO CAP 10-YEAR BOND YIELD AT 6.125% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines Tuesday rejected some bids at auction to lower the yield on a new 10-year treasury bond, just days after the government raised $1 billion from its maiden peso-denominated global bond. (published 0628 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par ROAD KING NOW SEEKS TO PRICE DOLLAR BOND TO YIELD AROUND 9.5%-9.625% - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Road King Infrastructure Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday tightened its price guidance for the planned US$300 million of U.S. dollar-denominated bonds, a person familiar with the situation said. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: INDONESIA AIMS FOR 66% RISE IN TRADE WITH CHINA IN 3-5 YEARS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia aims to increase its annual trade with China by more than 66% to $50 billion in three to five years from around $30 billion now after a free-trade agreement between the countries took full effect in January, Indonesia Trade Minister Mari Pangestu said Tuesday. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD PROMPT COPYCATS AROUND ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets might well fail to weaken the yen, but should have a near-term impact on other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =FOCUS: AUSTRALIAN HOUSING AFFORDABILITY CREATES POLICY HEADACHE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Big Four banks are likely to raise their mortgage rates beyond the amount of any new rate hikes from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , presenting the new Labor government with one of its first major policy challenges. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =PREVIEW: RBNZ TIPPED TO STAND PAT, HIGHLIGHT UNCERTAIN OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists widely expect the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to keep its Official Cash Rate unchanged at 3.0% Thursday, while highlighting the uncertain economic outlook in its accompanying statement, particularly after the 7.0-magnitude earthquake in the country's second-largest city of Christchurch earlier this month. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \uc2 \f2 DOWNER EDI\f28 \uc2 \f2  RAIL JV CREDIT RATING CUT; NO PLANS TO INJECT EQUITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Downer EDI Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that "it is not obligated" to provide further equity to the Reliance Rail consortium, of which it owns 49%, after Moody's Investors Service downgraded the consortium's credit rating again. (published 0522 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: ACE BUYS MALAYSIA'S JERNEH INSURANCE TO GROW ASIAN PRESENCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In a move to bolster its Asian presence, U.S. insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 ACE Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday agreed to buy Malaysian non-life insurer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jerneh Insurance Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for MYR654 million . (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: QANTAS ATTEMPTS TO BLOCK FAST APPROVAL OF \f28 \uc2 \f2 VIRGIN BLUE\f28 \uc2 \f2 , ETIHAD PACT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Qantas Airways Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has urged Australia's competition regulator to oppose calls by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Virgin Blue Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . to fast-track its proposed alliance with Abu Dhabi-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Etihad Airways\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0610 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =AIR INDIA EXECUTIVE: DELIVERY OF BOEING DREAMLINERS FURTHER DELAYED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The delivery of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Boeing Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s much-delayed 787 Dreamliner planes to Air India will be extended by two-three months more due to the cascading effect of another change in the U.S. plane maker's global delivery schedule, said a senior executive at the national carrier. (published 0516 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: UNITED SPIRITS TO BUY PIONEER DISTILLERIES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 United Spirits Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday said it has entered into an agreement to buy a majority stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Pioneer Distilleries Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for about INR740 million in a move aimed at raising its distillation capacity. (published 0459 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: RIO TINTO TO INVEST US$803M IN ARGYLE DIAMOND MINE UNDERGROUND PROJECT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Rio Tinto Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . will spend US$803 million ramping up production from its Argyle diamond mine in Western Australia state's Kimberley region as jewellery demand from burgeoning Asian markets depletes existing resources of the gemstones. (published 0426 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SK NETWORKS: TO ACQUIRE STAKE IN BRAZIL'S MMX FOR ABOUT $700 MILLION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's \f28 \uc2 \f2 SK Networks Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it has signed a non-binding agreement to acquire a stake in Brazilian iron ore mining company \f28 \uc2 \f2 MMX Mineracao e Metalicos SA\f28 \uc2 \f2  for around $700 million. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA'S FIRB APPROVES A$2.7B TAKEOVER OF HEALTHSCOPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Foreign Investment Review Board has no objection to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Carlyle Group LP\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 TPG Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s A$2.7 billion takeover of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Healthscope Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the hospital operator said Tuesday. (published 0012 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MITSUI & CO\f28 \uc2 \f2 : IN DEAL WITH CHINA'S SHENHUA IN COAL BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mitsui & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it has agreed with Chinese coal producer \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shenhua Group Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on wide-ranging cooperation in the coal business from distribution to overseas mine development, chemical production from coal and efficiency of coal usage. (published 0219 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA RESOURCES GAS TO BUY PARENT'S CITY GAS UNIT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Resources Gas Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is seeking to raise up to HK$2.52 billion via a share placement to fund its acquisition of an urban gas-distribution business from its parent, \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Resources Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  Group, according to a term sheet seen by Dow Jones Newswires on Tuesday. (published 0349 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TRICOM INDIA\f28 \uc2 \f2  TO BUY US-BASED HEALTHCARE SERVICE PROVIDER GTESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tricom India Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it agreed to acquire U.S.-based healthcare service provider GTESS Corp. through its unit Tricom Infotech Solutions Inc. (published 0404 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: SINGAPORE BOURSE TO LAUNCH NEW BOARD WITH ADRS OF 19 FIRMS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday its new board, GlobalQuote, will begin \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Oct. 22 with the American depositary receipts of 19 major Asian companies, in the latest attempt by the bourse to boost trading volumes and liquidity. (published 0632 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INTERVIEW: APOLLO HOSPITALS IN TIE-UP TALKS WITH KHAZANAH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Apollo Hospitals Enterprise Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . is in talks with Malaysian sovereign wealth fund \f28 \uc2 \f2 Khazanah Nasional Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for possible collaborations in health-care delivery and medical education in India and the rest of Asia, a top executive at the company said. (published 0643 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE:ASIAN SHARES MIXED; TOKYO CAUTIOUS BEFORE DPJ BALLOT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Asian stock markets were mixed Tuesday with investors in Tokyo turning cautious as Japan's ruling party held a ballot to decide its leader and thus the prime minister. (published 0406 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES:\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par UPDATE: MITSUI, SHENHUA FORGE ALLIANCE TO DEVELOP COAL BUSINESS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Mitsui & Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday it has forged an alliance with Chinese mining giant \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shenhua Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  to expand its coal business, including the possible development of Mongolia's massive coal reserves. (published 0654 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par AUSTRALIA MINISTER HAS AGREED TO CONSIDER EXPLORATION IN MINING TAX \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Energy Minister Martin Ferguson said Tuesday his center-left Labor government has agreed to consider revisiting some aspects of a proposed tax on mining company profits, such as an exploration rebate. (published 0641 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JINCHUAN REVIVES TALKS OVER NONOC NICKEL MINES -INDUSTRY GROUP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Jinchuan Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has revived negotiations to develop the Nonoc nickel mines in the southern Philippines region of Mindanao and construct a refinery at the mine site, a senior industry official said Tuesday. (published 0418 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: AUSTRALIA 2010-11 WHEAT CROP FORECAST RAISED TO 25.1 MLN TONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-09-10 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia has revised up its official winter and summer crop production forecasts sharply, following average to above-average rainfall in the Eastern Australia province in recent months. Including substantially higher production of wheat, the bigger crop could raise the amount available for exports in the coming year. (published 0408 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =INDIA LIKELY TO AIM FOR RECORD WHEAT OUTPUT OF 82 MLN TONS - OFFICIAL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India will likely aim for a record wheat output of 82 million metric tons this crop year through June 2011, helped by good rainfall and water reserves climbing above the 10-year average, a senior farm ministry official said Tuesday. (published 0642 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: BPC GETS HSFO TERM OFFERS; $36/TON OVER SINGAPORE -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-run Bangladesh Petroleum Corp has received four offers around a premium of $36 a metric to Singapore quotes for its first-ever term fuel-oil import contract, scheduled to begin next year, a person with direct knowledge of the matter said Tuesday. (published 0608 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par NEW HOPE CORP ACQUIRES INTEREST IN COAL LIQUIFICATION TECHNOLOGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian coal miner \f28 \uc2 \f2 New Hope Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  will acquire up to 51% of a coal liquefaction company that aims to create synthetic crude oil and coking coal. (published 2315 GMT Monday) [ 14-09-10 0714GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 62550   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100914e69e000hn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
