\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =UPDATE: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREATENS \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  AS YEN HITS NEW 15-YEAR HIGH \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  threatened again Tuesday to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market after the yen pushed to a fresh 15-year high against the dollar, keeping traders on their toes ahead of a ruling party leadership election later in the day that could trigger more \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  volatility. (published 0316 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: CHINA YUAN HITS FRESH MODERN-ERA HIGH VS DOLLAR TUESDAY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit another high against the U.S. dollar Tuesday after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the dollar/yuan central parity rate lower for the third straight trading session amid the dollar's global weakness and growing U.S. pressure over Beijng's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0429 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA AUGUST BUSINESS CONFIDENCE INDEX UP 9 POINTS TO +11 -NAB \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australian business confidence rose strongly in August, according to a survey released Tuesday, despite a period of political uncertainty as the country was left wondering what the make-up of the next government would be. (published 0130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: NZ RETAIL SALES NO IMPETUS FOR RBNZ TO HIKE RATE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 New Zealand retail sales fell in July, failing to meet expectations and giving little impetus for the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to start hiking the official cash rate before December. (published 0224 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BANK INDONESIA OFFICIAL: SEPT ON-YEAR INFLATION LIKELY BELOW 6% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Indonesia's on-year inflation in September will likely ease below 6%, from 6.44% in August, but the full-year target of 6% seems "hard to achieve," Bank Indonesia deputy governor Hartadi Sarwono said Tuesday. (published 0341 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par NZ GOVERNMENT INTRODUCES BILL TO CREATE FINANCIAL MARKETS AUTHORITY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand government Tuesday introduced a bill to parliament to create Financial Markets Authority, a new regulator that will consolidate functions currently carried out by several different entities. (published 0243 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ AUGUST MEDIAN HOUSE PRICE NZ$350,000 VS NZ$349,000 JULY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Subdued home sales in August compared to July and relatively flat home prices, coupled with tepid retail sales data Tuesday, further underscore that the Reserve Bank of New Zealand will likely keep key rates on hold at 3.0% at Thursday's monetary-policy review. (published 2346 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par AUSTRALIA RMBS PERFORMANCE TO DETERIORATE SLIGHTLY IN 3Q - FITCH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The performance of prime Australian residential mortgage-backed securities will deteriorate slightly in the third quarter as a series of interest rate hikes filter through the market, said Fitch Ratings in a report Tuesday. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: BUSINESS GROUPS TO FIGHT US JOB PLANS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Multinational companies and small-business interests are working in concert to oppose some of the Obama administration's jobs proposals. (published 0008 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: S&P LIFTS ARGENTINA RATING ON CONTINUED EFFORTS TO LOWER DEBT \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services lifted its junk-level rating on Argentina, saying continued funding from public-sector agencies has reduced the level of capital-market debt maturing over the next two years. (published 0015 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par EUROPEAN AUGUST ONLINE RECRUITMENT UNCHANGED FROM JULY-MONSTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European online recruitment activity held steady in August from July as various economies tackle austerity budgets or take advantage of the last remaining months before government spending cuts and tax increases begin to bite, a survey showed Tuesday. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par DATA SNAP: UK AUGUST HOUSE PRICE BALANCE SLUMPS TO -32 VS JULY -8 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. house prices fell sharply in August by the largest single month drop since between April and May 1989, and to the lowest level in over a year as another increase in the number of properties for sale and a steeper drop in buyer demand pushed prices lower, the Royal Institution of Chartered Surveyors said Tuesday. (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UK CONSUMER CONFIDENCE STRENGTHENED IN AUGUST - NATIONWIDE BUILDING SOCIETY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.K. consumers became less pessimistic about the outlook for the economy, the jobs market and their future incomes during August, according to a monthly survey conducted by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nationwide Building Society\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 2301 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ROAD KING NOW SEEKS TO PRICE DOLLAR BOND TO YIELD AROUND 9.5%-9.625% - SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Road King Infrastructure Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Tuesday tightened its price guidance for the planned US$300 million of U.S. dollar-denominated bonds, a person familiar with the situation said. (published 0332 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ASIA: \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  COULD PROMPT COPYCATS AROUND ASIA \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets might well fail to weaken the yen, but should have a near-term impact on other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0355 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FOCUS: AUSTRALIAN HOUSING AFFORDABILITY CREATES POLICY HEADACHE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's Big Four banks are likely to raise their mortgage rates beyond the amount of any new rate hikes from the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , presenting the new Labor government with one of its first major policy challenges. (published 0255 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =PREVIEW: RBNZ TIPPED TO STAND PAT, HIGHLIGHT UNCERTAIN OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economists widely expect the Reserve Bank of New Zealand to keep its Official Cash Rate unchanged at 3.0% Thursday, while highlighting the uncertain economic outlook in its accompanying statement, particularly after the 7.0-magnitude earthquake in the country's second-largest city of Christchurch earlier this month. (published 0415 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =BIG PICTURE: US CANNOT BLAME GROWING CHINA FOR ITS WOES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Economic activity is not a zero-sum gain, but it is certain that some of the better-than-expected growth posted by China came at the expense of its emerging economy rivals as well as U.S. manufacturers. (published 1914 GMT) [ 14-09-10 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI000002010091