\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  ASIA:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan Intervention \highlight\uc2  Could Prompt Copycats Around Asia\b0\par\par\uc2 By David Roman   \par \uc2 A Dow Jones Newswires Column   \par \uc2 664 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 05:55\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--A Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets might well fail to weaken the yen, but should have a near-term impact on other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have ratcheted up their rhetoric against a strong yen as the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rises steadily, hitting a 15-year high against the dollar Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Some analysts say Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would embolden other Asian central banks, many of which have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily so far this year, to increase their own dollar purchases to protect their exporters. Likely candidates for a quick correction under that scenario would be the Taiwan dollar, Korean won and Singapore dollar, all \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  closely watched by their central banks.\par \par \uc2 Asian central banks "would be more likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 " after a potential Japanese move, as it "would make them more comfortable with \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Sean Callow, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with \uc2 Westpac\uc2 . "All Asian central banks keep an eye on what the others are doing; they haven't been shy about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  might become likelier if Ichiro Ozawa, a kingmaker in the ruling Democratic Party of Japan, wins an internal party election Tuesday to replace Naoto Kan as party leader and prime minister. Ozawa has espoused a more activist line to curb the yen and protect Japanese exporters.\par \par \uc2 That could become a matter of concern for Japan's competitors, including South Korea and Taiwan, which have taken market share from Japanese exporters in fields such as automobiles and electronics.\par \par \uc2 Over the past two years, as the yen rose 19% against the U.S. dollar, the Korean won has lost 5% against the greenback and the Taiwan dollar has been flat. That has helped those economies -- which grew more than 7% on-year in the second quarter, compared with 1.5% growth in Japan -- to recover faster from the global slowdown.\par \par \uc2 Westpac\uc2 's Callow said China's response to any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also would be key, as the Chinese yuan has become an increasingly relevant benchmark for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . With \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hectoring China to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  less to weaken the yuan, China could react to Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by slowing or even reversing the pace of yuan appreciation.\par \par \uc2 Singapore, where the local dollar rose to an all-time high against the greenback earlier this week, is another candidate to mirror any Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . A person familiar with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's thinking said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more likely to step in if Tokyo does.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, Indonesia could find it hard to increase its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As of last month Bank Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves stood at $81.3 billion, up 36% on the year -- among the world's largest gains -- as a result of sustained dollar purchasing in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 Bank Indonesia has expressed reservations about the quick buildup and announced several measures to increase monitoring of investment inflows in recent months, looking to find other ways to lessen pressure on the rupiah.\par \par \uc2 That's because Indonesia's high policy rates, now at 6.5%, make it more expensive to keep dollar reserves there than in other countries, as commercial banks must be paid interest in local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in exchange for keeping dollars with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (David Roman, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reporter, has been a Dow Jones correspondent since 2002, covering economic and corporate news. He can be reached at 65 6415 4045 or by e-mail: david.roman@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 (Costas Paris in Singapore contributed to this story.)\par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAsia@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 14-09-10 0355GMT ]\par \par \uc2 1187 4256 4258 5095   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100914e69e0006p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
