\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK: USD/JPY Falls, 83.00 Level Eyed - Dealer\b0\par\par\uc2 236 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 03:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0146 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/JPY may fall below 83.00 soon as investors actively buying JPY amid growing expectations that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in market if PM Kan stays in his post, says Masanobu Ishikawa, senior dealer at Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  & Ueda Harlow; "As speculation grows that Kan will remain prime minister, many investors appear to be buying the yen." Says buying broad-based among foreign, domestic financial institutions. Unless Kan shows strong commitment to curbing current appreciation of yen, investors "won't stop buying" JPY, he says. DPJ presidential race result likely around 0630-0700 GMT. Citibank Japan chief strategy Osamu Takashima also eyeing 83.00 for USD/JPY if Kan wins; adds, halt in recent gains in Europe, U.S. bond yields making USD, EUR less attractive; says Japan exporters also behind USD sales.\par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, EUR/JPY falling as investors take profits after recent surge caused by upward revision of euro-zone GDP growth forecast yesterday, strong China economic data at weekend, says Naoto Taikoji, senior dealer at \uc2 Shinkin \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . EUR/USD last 107.22. USD/JPY weaker at 83.36, though off 15-year low of 83.25 marked earlier in day. (tomoyuki.tachikawa@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 14-09-10 0146GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1012 1037 1085 5011 55117 75112   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100914e69e00036\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\p