\par\par \b \uc2 WORLD  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Trades Near 15-Year Low Against Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Bradley Davis   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 15:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--The dollar fell Tuesday to a 15-year low against the yen after the election of a new ruling party leader in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  led investors to believe \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's recent strength was less likely.\par \par \uc2 The greenback also slid below parity against the Swiss franc for the first time since December 2009, as solid Swiss economic fundamentals increase the chances, in some analysts' views, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  on Thursday will increase key interest rates.\par \par \uc2 By New York morning trading, the dollar had recovered from its overnight lows against its rivals, but failed to get much of a boost from better-than-expected U.S. retail sales, as investors continued to worry over the pace of the U.S. recovery, and the Federal Reserve's possible response to kickstart moribund growth.\par \par \uc2 "The data is not strong enough to help the U.S. dollar to the extent that it does not detract from market concerns that another dose of [stimulus] still lies in the wings for later this year," said Alan Ruskin, global head of G10 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2  in New York.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday morning, the euro was at $1.2850 from $1.2873 late Monday, according to EBS via CQG. The dollar was at Y83.28 from Y83.65, while the euro was at Y107.01 from Y107.66. The U.K. pound was at $1.5411 from $1.5429. The dollar was at CHF1.0039 from CHF1.0072.\par \par \uc2 The ICE Dollar Index, which tracks the greenback against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was at 81.903 from 81.870.\par \par \uc2 The dollar traded within striking distance of the 15-year low it hit overnight, Y83.07, on the back of Japanese Prime Minister Naoto Kan's hold onto power Tuesday. He handily defeated longtime powerbroker Ichiro Ozawa for leadership of the ruling party.\par \par \uc2 Ozawa had been a more vocal proponent than Kan of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to curb the strong yen and of ramping up public spending to boost the flagging recovery. Investors bid the yen higher on Kan's reelection, but \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  analysts said current yen levels against the greenback warranted caution.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains a risk as [the dollar] approaches Y80, even under Kan, and markets are likely to tread carefully from here," the \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2  analysts said.\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc also hit a major new milestone Tuesday, shooting up to parity against the dollar for the first time since a spell of broad-based dollar weakness in December 2009.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  has pursued an aggressive strategy of seeking to hold down its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past, in an effort to deflect deflationary pressures, which build as the strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  makes imports cheaper. Since June, it appears to have stepped back from that stance, noting that signs of deflation have disappeared.\par \par \uc2 With the Swiss \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meeting on Thursday to announce any changes to its monetary policy, "we expect the SNB to deliver a 25 [basis point] hike this week, against a virtually unanimous consensus for unchanged rates," said \uc2 UBS\uc2  analysts. "We argue that wage inflation and a potential real estate bubble are weighing heavier than franc strength," making a rate hike more likely.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the euro declined modestly against the dollar after a survey of expectations for German manufacturing dropped sharply, though views on current conditions improved.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   Canada Morning \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Canadian dollar was slightly higher Tuesday morning after getting a boost from the stronger-than-expected U.S. retail sales data for August.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.S. dollar traded at C$1.0263 from C$1.0272 late Monday. It touched a low at C$1.0247 immediately after the U.S. data, its lowest level since Aug. 6, according to EBS via CQG.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback has been under pressure against its Canadian counterpart in recent sessions, but traders see strong support for the U.S. unit in the C$1.0250 area.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Canada\f28 \uc2 \f2  Mark Carney will deliver the seventh annual Deutsche Bundesbank Lecture in Berlin, Germany, at 11:00 a.m EDT (1155 GMT).\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The text of his remarks will be released at 10:45 a.m. EDT (1445 GMT). Carney will hold a short media availability after the event.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Bradley Davis, Dow Jones Newswires; 212-416-2654;\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 bradley.davis@dowjones.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Don Curren in Toronto and Katie Martin in London contributed to this article.) [ 09-14-10 0912ET ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1033 1074 1158 1863 1865 20714 28038 4164   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100914e69e00094\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
