\par\par \b \uc2 MARKET TALK:  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Action Bets May Lift Japan Stocks - Analysts\b0\par\par\uc2 1,171 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2010\par 11:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in Singapore. 65 64154 140; \par MarketTalk@dowjones.com \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0930 GMT [Dow Jones] The likelihood that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to weaken JPY has actually risen with Kan's victory in DPJ race, even though Ozawa was viewed as more eager to depress the yen via \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , market analysts say. "As he (Kan) is elected (and the uncertainty about his position has cleared), it is unlikely that he sits back and does nothing about the yen's strength. There is a higher possibility that he will \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says Shoji Hirakawa, chief strategist at UBS Securities. Susumu Kato, chief economist at Calyon Credit Agricole, says gains for stocks "may not be realized by any domestic factors but an \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  decision." Adds if Kan administration decides to act and yen is pushed down near Y90 vs USD, Nikkei may trade in 9500-10,000 range; index ended at 9299.31. (ayai.tomisawa@dowjones.com)\f28 \par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [Dow Jones] Greek/German bond yield spreads move only a relatively small amount following the auction of EUR1.17Bln Greek T-bills Tuesday. The uniform yield set at 4.82% with a healthy bid-to-cover of 4.54. The 2-year Greek/German spread is 4.5bps wider on the day at 890bps from 888bps before the auction), the 5-year spread is 3.5bps tighter at 1044bps (from 1042 before the auction) and the 10-year spread is 9.5bps wider at 90.3bps (from 900bps before the auction). (nick.andrews@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0929 GMT [Dow Jones] The USD index breached its 55DMA at 82.73 and focus now turns to the 81.90-70 support and 200DMA says \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  analysts Karen Jones and Axel Rudolph. Originally the pair were looking for this area to hold but now say they are less convinced and a failure here will target the recent 80.085 low. Topside resistance will be found at 82.73 and 83.00. The USD index now trades at 81.973. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0927 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/PKR falls to 85.80 vs 85.85 Thursday; "there was some demand for import payments held up due to the long weekend, but these were offset by remittances that helped the rupee strengthen," says dealer. Financial markets were shut Friday, Monday for religious holiday. Tips 85.80-85.90 band for Wednesday. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0925 GMT [Dow Jones] Pakistan shares higher with banks, cement, petroleum stocks staging strong recovery after recent losses. KSE-100 index last +1.9% at 10,075.17. "The market remained positive from the beginning and maintained 10,000 level in anticipation of quick resolution of leverage product issue. Chairman of SECP is also visiting the exchange on Sept. 20 to discuss the issue," says dealer. SECP also holding its meetings tomorrow to take some decisions on margin trading issues, says Khalid Iqbal Siddique analyst at Invest and Finance Securities. Volume heavy, suggesting buying interest strong. \uc2 Nishat Mills Ltd\uc2  (NML.KA) +4.0% at PKR47.51, DGK Cement (DGKC.KA) +2.3% at PKR26.86. (djn.in@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [Dow Jones] KLCI ends +1.2% at fresh 32-month high of 1474.44 with techs (+2.2%), finance (+1.7%) stocks leading gains. Local dealer says investors remain bullish on expectations of more equity fund inflows amid rising MYR. Tips next key resistance at 1500. "KLCI may still try to punch into higher territory despite its bearish divergence indicators," says Maybank IB research. Adds, although market interest currently on blue chips, may rotate to mid-cap, lower-liners soon. Market breadth positive with 504 advancers vs 274 decliners. Among most actives, Maybank (1155.KU) +2.9% at MYR8.76, \uc2 IOI Corp\uc2  (1961.KU) +2.0% at MYR5.74, Genting (3182.KU) +4.4% at MYR9.99, JCY (5161.KU) +6.4% at MYR1.17, AirAsia (5099.KU) down 1.0% at MYR1.92. (kwan-por.lee@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0922 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds are at session highs despite Greece selling EUR1.17B of 26-month T-bills at a healthy bid-to-cover ratio and a yield under 5%. December bunds are up 0.73 at 130.64. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0918 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/IDR lower at 8,965 late vs 9,015 Wednesday as foreign fund inflows continue, dealers say. "I think the pair should be trading around IDR8,940, but the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying near IDR8,950," dealer says. Adds, Bank Indonesia may have bought around $10 million at 8,955 to stem IDR's strength. Pair tipped in 8,950-8,970 range for Wednesday. (andreasismar.sandiwan@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0906 GMT [Dow Jones] Bunds extend gains after the September ZEW economic expectations index prints at -4.3 vs expectations of 9.0. The annual rise in industrial production in the euro zone also eased to 7.1% in July, the slowest pace since February. December bunds are up 0.50 at 130.42. (neelabh.chaturvedi@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0906 GMT [Dow Jones] EUR/USD drops some 25 ticks to 1.2861 after a mixed August ZEW survey with current conditions sharply outperforming at 59.9 vs 44.7 forecast but economic expectations sharply underperforming at -4.3 against +14 seen. (gary.stride@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0905 GMT [Dow Jones] Markets likely to focus on new Cabinet lineup after PM Kan won ruling DPJ presidential election against powerful veteran lawmaker Ichiro Ozawa. "Investors are likely to continue taking a wait-and-see stance until the next Cabinet lineup is clear," says Fumiyuki Nakanishi, general manager at SMBC Friend Securities. "If the Ozawa group is left out (of new Cabinet), he won't be able to stay within the DPJ," he adds, noting possibility of increased uncertainty if Ozawa defection causes political realignment. Says stock market volume likely to remain low until October; active selling by hedge funds may briefly drag Nikkei below year-to-date intraday low of 8807.41 (logged on Aug. 25), which may then trigger government \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  into \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Nikkei 225 December futures down 0.6% at 9190. (kana.inagaki@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0902 GMT [Dow Jones] USD/TWD lower at 31.815 late vs 31.850 yesterday, after hovering in 31.72-31.75 band for most of session. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of buying late, may have bought around US$10 million-US$20 million to curb TWD strength, traders say. Still, "\b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's recent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  are smaller than what we saw in the past months. It appears to me the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is now more comfortable with the Taiwan dollar" because it's rising slowly, one trader says. Second trader says TWD likely to extend gains tomorrow; thinks USD/TWD may test 31.72 support. (aries.poon@dowjones.com) [ 09-14-10 0530ET ]\par \par \uc2 4022   \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020100914e69e0006m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
