\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 793 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 September 2010\par 07:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par =2ND UPDATE: BASEL COMMITTEE ANNOUNCES TIGHTER NEW CAPITAL STANDARDS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 International financial officials Sunday agreed to significantly increase the amount of capital banks have to set aside against potential losses, but gave them several years to adapt to the new rules. (published 2130 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par YUAN HITS MODERN-ERA HIGH ON RECORD LOW FIXING, GEITHNER REMARKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The yuan hit a modern-era high against the U.S. dollar Monday after China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  set the yuan's reference rate for daily trading at its strongest level against the dollar since it began publishing the daily fixing in 1994, amid increasing pressure from the U.S. over Beijing's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy. (published 0359 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: ECONOMIC FORECASTING SURVEY: 3 IN 5 EXPECT FED TO RESUME SECURITIES PURCHASES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Three in five of economists surveyed by The Wall Street Journal expect the Federal Reserve to resume large-scale purchases of securities in the face of a deteriorating economic outlook--but by a 3-to-2 margin most of them also think that would be a mistake. (published 0400 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN FSA: BASEL CAPITAL RULES ACHIEVABLE FOR DOMESTIC BANKS -KYODO \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's banking regulator said that new capital standards agreed Sunday by the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision are achievable for domestic banks, Kyodo News reported Monday. (published 0314 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA: NEW BASEL STANDARDS TO HAVE MINIMAL IMPACT ON DOMESTIC BANKS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean government said Monday that the new capital standards announced by the Basel Committee on Banking Supervision Sunday will have a minimal impact on domestic banks. (published 0106 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: CHINA'S ECONOMY RESUMES ACCELERATION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China's major economic indicators picked up in August after slowing for several months, data issued over the weekend show, an unexpected rebound that could help prospects for global growth. (published 1737 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S KOREA AUGUST IMPORT PRICES +0.3% ON MONTH; RAW MATERIAL PRICES UP \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea's import prices rebounded in August from the previous month as higher prices of grain and raw materials offset the soothing effect of the won's appreciation against the dollar. (published 0300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =UPDATE: NZ EARTHQUAKE TO REDUCE 3Q GDP BY AROUND 0.4% - TREASURY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The New Zealand Treasury said Monday the 7.0-magnitude quake in the country's second-largest city of Christchurch will reduce gross domestic product by 0.4% in the September quarter, but recovery efforts will then boost the economy. (published 0326 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OZAWA MIGHT CARRY OUT \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  THREAT IF ELECTED PM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Politicians often find it hard to fulfil their campaign promises when they confront the realities of governing after winning office. (published 0340 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par PHILIPPINES TO REVIEW TREASURY AUCTION PLAN FOR 4Q - NATIONAL TREASURER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' Treasury will review its domestic borrowing plan for the fourth quarter following the successful issuance of its maiden peso-denominated global bonds, National Treasurer Roberto Tan said Monday. (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par KOREA FINANCE CORP TO ISSUE DOLLAR BOND LATER THIS WEEK -SOURCE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned policy financing arm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea Finance Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . plans to issue a dollar-denominated bond later this week to raise between $500 million and $750 million, a person familiar with the situation said Monday. (published 0250 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 KOREA NATIONAL OIL CORP\f28 \uc2 \f2  PLANS TO RAISE $500 MLN-$1 BLN VIA BOND ISSUE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 State-owned \f28 \uc2 \f2 Korea National Oil Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Monday that it plans to raise between $500 million and $1 billion by issuing foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 -denominated bonds sometime this year. (published 0141 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    ======== DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======== \par  \par  \par =WORLD \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : EURO UP VS DOLLAR, YEN AFTER CHINA DATA, BASEL \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The euro rose against the dollar and yen in Asia Monday as investors speculated that a pickup in Chinese economic growth, as reflected in data over the weekend, would buoy risk-sensitive assets such as the common \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the months ahead. (published 0424 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =FOCUS: JAPAN OZAWA'S \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , FUNDING TALK WOULD FACE MAJOR TESTS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many investors are doubtful. Their concerns are mounting as the ruling-Democratic Party of Japan power-broker tries to oust Prime Minister Naoto Kan as party president in a Sept. 14 election in which only party members vote. Polls suggest the vote could go either way. (published 2300 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par =WSJ: JAPAN ELECTION TO BE STRONGLY FELT BY FINANCIAL MARKETS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 If market players like volatility, they should be rooting for a victory by Ichiro Ozawa in the race to be Japan's Prime Minister. (published 2343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  OPTIONS: DOLLAR/YEN OPTIONS UP AHEAD OF DPJ ELECTION \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar/yen options rose in Tokyo Monday, as demand for protection against sharp falls in the yen increased ahead of a ruling party election in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that could increase the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0405 GMT) [ 13-09-10 0500GMT ]\f28 \par \par \uc2 1030 1804 4180   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020100913e69d00096\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
